CORINE Land Cover test data in this directory
=============================================

Both files below are derived from CORINE Land Cover 2018 (CLC2018), produced by
the Copernicus Land Monitoring Service and distributed by the European
Environment Agency (EEA).

  (c) European Union, Copernicus Land Monitoring Service 2018,
  European Environment Agency (EEA).

Produced with funding by the European Union. Access to the data is free, full
and open under Regulation (EU) No 1159/2013 (the Copernicus data policy; the
governing act is now Regulation (EU) 2021/696). Its conditions, per the EEA's
catalogue record for CLC2018 vector v2020_20u1
(sdi.eea.europa.eu/catalogue/copernicus/api/records/71c95a07-e296-44fc-b22b-415f42acfdf0):
inform the public of the source; state clearly where the data were adapted or
modified; do not suggest that the European Union endorses this use. Both files
below are modified, as each entry says. Neither the European Union nor the EEA
endorses this project or its use of the data.


1. clc2018_7908_3.gpkg (increment 16b, 2026-09-28)
--------------------------------------------------

Source: CORINE Land Cover 2018, vector, version v2020_20u1 (the GeoPackage
U2018_CLC2018_V2020_20u1.gpkg, layer U2018_CLC2018_V2020_20u1, EPSG:3035).

Modified: selected and clipped. The features whose R-tree box meets the
EPSG:3035 image of the committed benchmark tile's node rectangle
(dem_archive/7908_3_10m_z33.tif, EPSG:25833) are kept, each clipped in
EPSG:3035 to that image buffered by 1 km, and re-encoded as a small GeoPackage
with the source's table, columns, spatial reference row and R-tree index. The
coordinates are not reprojected; the tests reproject them. Written by
extract.py in this directory, which is reproducible from the source file.


2. 0000_4326_corine2018_4e6064_GML.gml (legacy test data)
---------------------------------------------------------

Origin: added to this repository on 2020-03-12 in commit 8e30af4, "Adding data
for small test", together with dem_archive/7908_3_10m_z33.tif (the benchmark
tile), as the legacy `ingoya_test` pair (legacy/tests/test_gml_repository.py).
It came in with no attribution; this notice supplies it (Ola's ruling on
increment 16b's Q6, 2026-09-28).

Content: 200 CORINE Land Cover 2018 polygons over northern Norway in EPSG:4326,
in a Norwegian redistribution's schema (attributes clc18_kode and sl_sdeid),
written by OGR as GML 2 (gml:coordinates).

Modified (before it reached this repository): selected, reprojected to
EPSG:4326 and re-encoded as GML.

Modified (in this repository, increment 16b, 2026-09-28): repaired to be
well-formed XML (Ola: "Repear the broken file."). As committed in 2020 the
file lacked a </gml:featureMember> after feature sql_statement.40965 (line
1097) and ended without closing its root element. repair_gml.py in this
directory adds exactly those two closing tags and changes nothing else; it
runs only on the 2020 file (git blob 97ddc98, commit 8e30af4) and is
reproducible from it, as its docstring shows. The reader in
src_python/tin_engine/io/gml.py is strict and reads the repaired file.
